{"request_sha256": "c41ddba4876c03e6ed16887186db8a7b10b82cc24da9cd1f4e86a02170f6259d", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "3a695aff7ad41c11d02a326b9a770e36cf77004e761dcaa0f3a4350a3d7f3ece", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 12608}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["owner-fronds-long-arching (seeds 1 and 42): the crown is a flat radiating star of very short, very thin, sparsely-leafleted axes; no frond arches, none droop below the crown base, and frond length is a small fraction of trunk length — the reference crown is a rounded shuttlecock of long arching fronds whose lowest members hang well below the insertion point.", "owner-trunk-straight-constant (seeds 1 and 42): the trunk carries abrupt lateral kinks (an upper bend below the crown and a pronounced step near mid-height) plus a continuous taper from a wide ground flare to a narrow apex; this reads as wavy and non-constant, not the straight or gently-leaning constant-diameter column of the references.", "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds: leaflets render as isolated dark specks along a visibly bare rachis; the frond does not read as a continuous once-pinnate blade, and frond count appears far below the 30-60 of the reference crown.", "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern and trunk-fibrous-matting: the drawn trunk in P-TRUNK is a smooth untextured cylinder with no leaf-base stubs, no spiral lattice and no fibre. Reported against what is drawn, not inferred from the un-landed fn-110 work.", "leaf-base-close (P-BASE, render-3): the frame is an extreme close-up almost entirely filled by an unlit near-black trunk surface; no leaf-base geometry, stub faces or fibre can be resolved either way. Unassessable, not absent.", "fruit-clusters-pendent: no pendent fruiting bunches are present. Owner has explicitly descoped fn-111 for this pass, so this is recorded rather than counted as a blocker for the current gate.", "dead-frond-skirt, petiole-base-orange-sheath, trunk-colour-and-weathering: all absent from the render; the trunk is a flat uniform dark brown with no weathered stub faces and no rust-orange crown-base material.", "crown-silhouette-proportions: frond length is a very small fraction of visible trunk length, so the tree reads as a pole with a tuft rather than a mature date palm silhouette."], "observations": ["Three of the four owner-priority P-WHOLE requirements fail on both seeds; seeds 1 and 42 differ only in kink placement and crown rotation, so the failures are not seed-specific.", "The only supported owner priority is owner-trunk-bare: in both P-WHOLE renders and in P-TRUNK the trunk carries no foliage, epiphytes, offshoots or branches of any kind.", "The spruce anchor (anchor-0) was used only to gauge finish level. Leaflet rendering in the candidate is markedly sparser and more aliased than the anchor's continuous needle mass, so the finish floor is not clearly met either — recorded as an observation, and the anchor carries no morphology weight.", "Reference-1 and reference-2 show epiphytic ferns on the trunk; the inventory treats these as scene features, and their absence from the candidate is not counted against it.", "The inventory's trunk-lean-and-curve entry admits strong lean and S-curvature as variation. The candidate's deviation is not that: it is a stepped kink with a discontinuity in the silhouette, which the owner priority rules out explicitly.", "P-BASE is a genuine unknown, not a concealed fail: the joint input marks render-3 visibility 'hidden' and the pixels confirm the subject fills the frame in near-total shadow.", "Whether the crown deficit is dial-limited (leaflet size / frond length, per the owner's note) or structural is not determined by these images; no mechanism is asserted.", "Relative improvement over any earlier state was not assessable here and would not substitute for absolute readiness in any case."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown is a flat radial star of short, thin, sparsely-leafleted axes; no arching, no drooping lower fronds, frond length a small fraction of trunk length. Identical at seed 1 and seed 42.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with the owner's reading that leaflet size and frond length dials are set far too low, but the images alone do not distinguish a dial limit from a structural one."}, {"observation": "Trunk silhouette shows abrupt lateral kinks at upper and mid height plus continuous taper from a broad ground flare to a narrow apex.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The kinks resemble segment-boundary discontinuities in a swept trunk curve, and the taper resembles a tip-taper parameter at 1.0, which the host notes is outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range. Neither is established by the renders."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface as drawn is a smooth untextured cylinder: no leaf-base stubs, no spiral diamond lattice, no fibrous matting, no weathering variation.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Owner states fn-110 (trunk organs) is not landed; recorded as a mismatch against what is drawn rather than excused."}, {"observation": "Trunk bears no foliage, epiphytes, branches or offshoots anywhere along its length in either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "P-BASE frame is filled by an unlit near-black trunk surface; no leaf-base geometry resolvable in either direction.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Close camera placement with the subject in its own shade; exposure and framing are candidate causes, neither established."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruiting bunches are present below the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Owner has explicitly scoped the date cluster (fn-111) out of this first pass."}, {"observation": "Foliage colour is mid-to-deep green, inside the range spanned by reference-0 (deep green) and reference-1/2 (grey-glaucous).", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No crownshaft is drawn; frond bases sit directly on the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Leaflet rendering is sparse and aliased into isolated dark specks, visibly below the continuous, evenly-lofted foliage mass of the fn9 spruce anchor used as the finish-quality floor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "anchor-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Could be leaflet count/size, could be sampling or alpha behaviour at this resolution; not determinable from these frames. Anchor bears on finish only, never morphology."}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Reference crowns are rounded shuttlecocks of many long fronds, newest erect and older progressively recurved, the lowest hanging below the crown base. The candidate crown is a near-planar radiating star of short straight axes with no recurvature and nothing drooping below the insertion point. Defining mismatch on both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Reference leaflets are narrow, stiff and densely inserted in groups, giving a plumose V-sectioned frond with a bristly margin. In the candidate the leaflets are isolated specks widely spaced along a visible bare rachis; no plumose section or continuous blade reads at any of the three render scales."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "render-1", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The trunk as drawn in P-TRUNK is a smooth untextured cylinder; no stubs, no spiral, no diamond lattice, and no knobbly texture even at the P-WHOLE distance where the references still show it. Assessed on what is drawn; fn-110 not being landed explains the absence but does not convert it into a match. P-BASE could not corroborate (unlit)."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No reddish-brown fibre, husk or shaggy interstitial material anywhere on the candidate trunk; the surface is a single flat brown gradient."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The 'single unbranched' half matches — one stem, no branching anywhere. The 'roughly constant diameter' half does not: the candidate tapers continuously from a broad basal flare to a markedly narrower apex and carries stepped kinks. Constant diameter is part of this trait's defining character, so the trait fails rather than partially passing."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No pendent bunches, stalks or fruit mass in either P-WHOLE seed, where they would be visible if drawn. Explicitly recorded as a core reference trait that is absent; the owner has descoped fn-111 for this pass, so it is not treated as a blocker for the current gate, but it is not dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary. Reference-0 shows a brown collar of collapsed dead fronds beneath the living crown; the candidate crown-to-trunk transition is abrupt and entirely bare."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait. Candidate foliage reads mid-to-deep green, inside the deep-green to grey-glaucous span the inventory records across the three references. No mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. P-TRUNK resolves the crown apex well enough to show the frond bases; they are uniform dark green/brown with no pale petioles and no rust-orange fibrous sheath material."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The inventory admits both a strong smooth S-curve and a straight vertical stem as variation. The candidate's deviation is neither: it is a stepped, kinked profile with visible silhouette discontinuities on both seeds. Against the owner's authoritative 'never wavy', this is defining character, not acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, which the inventory flags as a scene feature rather than species character (absent in reference-0). The candidate's bare trunk sits inside that range and directly satisfies the owner's 'nothing grows on the trunk'."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary. References show grey-brown to warm reddish-brown with lighter, greyer, partly bleached stub faces against darker fibre. The candidate trunk is a single flat dark brown with only a lighting gradient; P-BASE is too dark to add anything."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The inventory records this trait as uncertain (reference-0 resolves only a broad rooted base merging into a soil mound). The candidate does widen at ground level, but that widening is the bottom of a continuous full-height taper rather than a localised basal flare, so it does not support the trait. Fail on grounds of the taper, with the inventory's own uncertainty noted."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary. No smooth green columnar sheath between crown and trunk in the candidate; frond bases sit directly on the stem, as in reference-1."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and flagged uncertain in the inventory itself (resolution limits separating true spines from short rigid leaflets in the references). The candidate's proximal rachis regions are drawn at too few pixels, and its leaflets are uniformly speck-like along the whole rachis, so neither presence nor absence of a distinct proximal spine zone can be read. Missing evidence, not a match."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Variation trait, flagged uncertain in the inventory because ratios shift with viewing distance. Even allowing that latitude, the candidate's frond length is a very small fraction of visible trunk length and the crown reads as a tuft on a pole, outside any plausible reading of the references. Same underlying deficit as owner-fronds-long-arching."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"6b9f8ff2-5eb5-44f7-91c7-532cd9526c97","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","workflow-launch-exec","reload-plugins","reload-skills","rename","ultrareview","security-review","usage-credits","extra-usage","usage","insights","recap","skill-doctor","goal","design-consent","design-revoke","list-agents","team-onboarding"],"terminal_slash_commands":["doctor","color","reload-plugins"],"apiKeySource":"none","claude_code_version":"2.1.278","output_style":"default","agents":["claude","Explore","general-purpose","Plan"],"skills":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator"],"plugins":[{"name":"flow-next","path":"/home/daniel/.claude-profiles/danithekiller93/plugins/cache/flow-next/flow-next/6.